{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** You're given `points[i] = [x, y]` on a plane. Joining two points costs their **Manhattan distance**, `|x₁ - x₂| + |y₁ - y₂|`. Return the minimum total cost to connect all the points, so that there's exactly one route between any two of them."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/e622d270-02a3-445a-8c89-cb9e0ee1933c.svg",
      "alt": "Five points: (0,0), (2,2), (3,10), (5,2) and (7,0). The cheapest way to connect them uses four links: (0,0)-(2,2) for 4, (2,2)-(5,2) for 3, (5,2)-(7,0) for 4 and (2,2)-(3,10) for 9. Total 20.",
      "width": 797,
      "height": 455,
